WEBVTT

00:57.432 --> 00:58.558
Then why are you here?

00:58.641 --> 01:01.770
If not for money or sex,
what are you here for?

01:03.730 --> 01:04.814
I was hoping

01:08.276 --> 01:09.652
I could see you

01:10.987 --> 01:11.821
again.

01:13.823 --> 01:14.657
Your eyes.

01:16.910 --> 01:18.578
I wanted to see them again.

01:21.581 --> 01:22.415
My eyes?

01:23.917 --> 01:24.751
Your eyes

01:26.878 --> 01:29.089
remind me of someone I used to know.

01:31.883 --> 01:32.884
Who is that person?

01:35.136 --> 01:36.471
Someone who's messed up.

01:38.264 --> 01:39.724
Help me. Help!

01:43.436 --> 01:44.312
Shall I help him?

01:49.567 --> 01:50.485
Or not?

02:05.959 --> 02:06.793
Wait.

02:14.551 --> 02:15.510
A woman

02:18.471 --> 02:19.806
whose eyes

02:21.141 --> 02:22.308
utterly lacked warmth.

02:29.357 --> 02:30.400
That woman...

02:34.654 --> 02:36.197
Were you afraid of her?

02:40.285 --> 02:41.202
No, the opposite.

03:40.845 --> 03:41.846
I liked her.

03:51.689 --> 03:55.693
CHAPTER 2
THE LADY IN RED SHOES

03:55.777 --> 04:00.114
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

04:01.741 --> 04:04.911
Are you making a move on me now?

04:07.413 --> 04:10.541
I remind you of the girl
in your beautiful memories?

04:12.001 --> 04:13.670
I never said they were beautiful.

04:30.186 --> 04:32.563
Do you still like me?

04:39.612 --> 04:40.655
Don't get it wrong.

04:41.864 --> 04:43.199
They're not good memories.

04:44.742 --> 04:45.576
Is that so?

04:49.914 --> 04:50.832
But you know what?

04:51.666 --> 04:53.126
Bad memories

04:54.043 --> 04:57.088
stay here longer.

05:11.060 --> 05:14.063
Hey, I can't believe
you let them run into each other!

05:14.147 --> 05:15.523
You should've stopped her.

05:15.857 --> 05:18.735
Well, Ms. Ko showed up unannounced.

05:19.402 --> 05:20.987
Does she ever give us a heads-up?

05:21.070 --> 05:22.530
Gosh, seriously.

05:22.989 --> 05:26.034
If you lack foresight,
you should've fought with all your might.

05:26.117 --> 05:27.994
Unbelievable! Why do I even pay you?

05:32.081 --> 05:33.916
I want to punch him, even just once.

05:40.631 --> 05:44.135
Go tell Mr. Lee that I understand
how tough his job must be.

05:44.218 --> 05:45.053
What?

05:45.386 --> 05:48.056
But he doesn't need
to go to such lengths for me,

05:48.139 --> 05:49.724
so tell him not to call me again.

05:57.440 --> 05:58.900
My gosh.

05:59.692 --> 06:02.403
I'm very late, aren't I?
The traffic was awful.

06:02.487 --> 06:04.530
How about we talk
over some sweet beverage?

06:04.614 --> 06:06.074
No, it's okay.

06:06.532 --> 06:07.909
Oh, you're leaving already?

06:07.992 --> 06:09.952
Don't forget to get Ms. Ko's autograph.

06:14.082 --> 06:15.625
My autograph?

06:15.708 --> 06:17.794
- Well, that's--
- Earlier, you asked me

06:17.877 --> 06:20.755
to get Ms. Ko's autograph for you.

06:24.425 --> 06:26.094
The spiel about my eyes

06:26.177 --> 06:29.097
and that girl in your memories

06:30.139 --> 06:31.557
was all for my autograph?

06:33.309 --> 06:34.143
No.

06:34.227 --> 06:35.937
So you weren't after money or sex.

06:36.020 --> 06:38.398
My autograph was what you wanted.

06:39.107 --> 06:40.024
I said, no.

06:40.108 --> 06:41.859
My gosh, this is perfect.

06:41.943 --> 06:43.820
We can call this
an impromptu fan meeting.

06:43.903 --> 06:46.280
- Why don't we drink this--
- I'll give you one.

06:46.364 --> 06:47.323
My autograph.

06:54.539 --> 06:56.749
This is my newest book, hot off the press.

06:59.043 --> 06:59.919
All right.

07:01.254 --> 07:02.505
Name?

07:06.467 --> 07:07.301
Name?

07:10.304 --> 07:11.139
Moon...

07:12.723 --> 07:13.558
Sang-tae.

07:16.102 --> 07:17.728
Who's Sang-tae? Is he your nephew?

07:18.771 --> 07:20.314
No, he's my brother.

07:20.398 --> 07:24.277
I see. Your brother is a fan of hers.

07:25.027 --> 07:27.780
Right, Mun-yeong has fans of all ages
and nationalities.

07:27.864 --> 07:30.616
She has a huge fanbase.

07:30.700 --> 07:31.826
Congratulations.

07:31.909 --> 07:33.703
- Consider these fan goods--
- Here.

07:37.707 --> 07:39.750
ZOMBIE KID

07:45.214 --> 07:46.215
I'll be off, then.

07:47.216 --> 07:48.301
See you again.

07:52.680 --> 07:53.556
I don't think so.

07:55.766 --> 07:58.269
Gosh, I have to make sure he takes this.

07:58.686 --> 07:59.562
Mr. Moon!

08:00.396 --> 08:01.856
Mr. Moon.

08:02.565 --> 08:05.985
Mr. Moon, please. Hold on a second.

08:06.068 --> 08:07.778
Goodness, just a second--

08:08.696 --> 08:10.198
Gosh, my apologies.

08:10.865 --> 08:15.411
I'm truly sorry about what happened,
so please take this.

08:19.582 --> 08:22.293
50,000 WON

08:23.461 --> 08:25.046
This is too much for myself.

08:25.129 --> 08:27.840
Well, then you can share it
with the people around you.

08:28.341 --> 08:29.300
- Oh, I see.
- Yes.

08:30.384 --> 08:31.719
Shall I do that, then?

08:33.179 --> 08:35.473
Gosh, hey! No!

08:35.556 --> 08:37.308
Hey, don't... Hey!

08:44.774 --> 08:45.733
Hey, jeez.

08:47.944 --> 08:50.738
I don't need this, so don't follow me.

08:52.448 --> 08:54.242
But... Wait.

08:58.287 --> 09:00.998
I've been cleaning up after Mun-yeong
for ten years,

09:01.082 --> 09:02.917
and no one has ever said no to this.

09:03.960 --> 09:05.002
What an oddball.

09:06.254 --> 09:08.172
Gosh, I have a bad feeling about this.

09:09.549 --> 09:11.259
Should I have offered him two boxes?

09:27.942 --> 09:28.859
Beautiful.

09:32.321 --> 09:33.197
I want him.

10:00.558 --> 10:01.642
I want him.

10:02.560 --> 10:03.561
I want him.

10:13.821 --> 10:15.615
Did you ask for me?

10:21.621 --> 10:23.789
You said you want to be given
a proper task.

10:24.874 --> 10:28.085
Yes, just tell me what you need.
I'll do anything.

10:28.586 --> 10:31.589
Do some digging on the man who just left.

10:35.343 --> 10:37.845
- Pardon?
- If you tell Mr. Lee,

10:40.097 --> 10:42.600
I'll pull out your tongue,
so keep this a secret.

10:53.402 --> 10:57.281
ZOMBIE KID
KO MUN-YEONG'S NEWEST BOOK, COMING SOON

10:59.158 --> 11:00.785
ZOMBIE KID

11:04.330 --> 11:05.414
JAE-SU

11:07.917 --> 11:08.834
Yes, we're eating.

11:09.919 --> 11:13.964
Your landlady stopped by
early in the morning and lashed out at me.

11:16.175 --> 11:18.052
Gross. It has your saliva on it.

11:18.135 --> 11:19.595
It's gross. Your saliva.

11:19.679 --> 11:22.890
Cover your mouth when you cough.
It's better than catching a virus.

11:24.767 --> 11:26.352
Yes, he's doing great.

11:27.812 --> 11:28.729
I mean, so far.

11:30.106 --> 11:33.317
Hey, where did you go?
Are you working as a driver or something?

11:35.027 --> 11:35.986
What? Ko Mun-yeong?

11:38.364 --> 11:40.199
What? Her autograph?

11:45.538 --> 11:46.414
Okay, bye.

11:52.128 --> 11:53.254
He got it.

11:53.337 --> 11:54.463
Gosh, hold on!

11:54.547 --> 11:56.590
Wait up. Can't we finish the food?

11:57.007 --> 11:58.759
Hey! Wait!

12:06.767 --> 12:09.812
Dear Sang-tae. I hope you can come
to my book launch party.

12:09.895 --> 12:12.314
You can get my autograph
and take pictures with me.

12:12.398 --> 12:14.316
We'll have fun.

12:14.400 --> 12:18.404
Mun-yeong will be waiting for you.
Wink!

12:19.238 --> 12:21.115
Jeez, what's wrong with her?

12:24.326 --> 12:26.036
RETAIL SPACE FOR LEASE

12:26.120 --> 12:27.496
Where do you need me to go?

12:28.372 --> 12:29.665
Well...

12:30.624 --> 12:32.877
I have to finish packing,

12:32.960 --> 12:35.755
go persuade my landlady, and--

12:35.838 --> 12:37.923
I want an outfit
that'll make me look smart

12:38.007 --> 12:40.718
like an Oxford University student.

12:40.801 --> 12:43.387
I should also tie up loose ends
at all my part-time jobs.

12:44.096 --> 12:47.016
Are you pulling webs
out of a spider's butt? Stop rambling on.

12:47.099 --> 12:49.101
So you want me to take Sang-tae

12:49.185 --> 12:51.395
to that woman's signing event, right?

12:52.354 --> 12:53.189
Yes.

12:54.648 --> 12:57.359
All right. Text me the time and location.

12:59.028 --> 13:00.029
Thanks, Jae-su.

13:00.821 --> 13:02.656
Who's your favorite, me or Sang-tae?

13:10.414 --> 13:13.250
You're so shy. You're such a cutie pie!

13:16.045 --> 13:17.004
Hello!

13:21.884 --> 13:23.010
Ju-ri.

13:26.722 --> 13:28.307
Another fried chicken place?

13:33.854 --> 13:35.231
Are you that excited?

13:35.314 --> 13:38.692
"Dear Sang-tae!

13:38.776 --> 13:41.529
I hope you can come
to my book launch party.

13:41.946 --> 13:44.657
You can get my autograph
and take pictures with me.

13:44.740 --> 13:46.951
We'll have fun.

13:47.034 --> 13:50.079
Mun-yeong will be waiting for you. Wink!"

13:51.622 --> 13:55.334
"Dear Sang-tae!" Yes!

13:56.043 --> 13:58.170
Okay, Oxford University student.

13:58.671 --> 14:00.631
My gosh, this is nice.

14:08.013 --> 14:09.640
Sang-tae, try this one.

14:10.349 --> 14:11.725
Yes, this one's cool.

14:19.483 --> 14:21.110
Looking cool...

14:22.111 --> 14:25.531
What do I do with my face to look cool?

14:26.699 --> 14:28.158
Cool facial expressions.

14:28.993 --> 14:30.369
How do I look cool?

14:43.966 --> 14:45.384
Cool facial expressions.

14:54.560 --> 14:55.895
- Beer's on the house.
- Well…

14:55.978 --> 14:58.314
I have to go back this evening,
so I can't drink.

14:58.397 --> 14:59.899
- How about Coke?
- Sure.

15:06.864 --> 15:08.032
It's also on the house.

15:13.954 --> 15:16.457
I heard you moved
to a hospital in the countryside.

15:17.583 --> 15:18.751
Right.

15:19.960 --> 15:21.795
RETAIL SPACE FOR LEASE

15:21.879 --> 15:25.215
By the way, are you moving again?

15:25.633 --> 15:28.677
Well, you know.
I refuse to be tied down to one place.

15:28.761 --> 15:30.846
I'm like the last nomad in this country.

15:50.658 --> 15:53.202
Well... All is good, right?

15:53.869 --> 15:55.496
Yes, as you can see.

15:56.830 --> 15:57.665
No, I mean...

15:59.500 --> 16:00.417
Gang-tae.

16:04.088 --> 16:07.716
Yes. He's doing well,
getting joy out of overworking himself.

16:13.430 --> 16:14.431
Are you hurt?

16:15.766 --> 16:16.600
No, I'm okay.

16:16.684 --> 16:20.062
Take it easy. Your wage won't go up
even if you work that hard.

16:20.145 --> 16:23.607
They say one must seek out hard work
while still young, but that's bullshit.

16:23.691 --> 16:26.193
Gosh, you'll see when you're older.

16:26.819 --> 16:30.030
You'll suffer from body aches all over
and get sick all the time.

16:37.621 --> 16:40.207
That young man is so unyielding.

17:08.902 --> 17:10.654
All right, let's start the meeting.

17:10.738 --> 17:11.697
- Okay.
- Yes, sir.

17:12.823 --> 17:14.783
I'll start with the reviews.

17:15.159 --> 17:16.493
Most reviewers said

17:16.577 --> 17:20.622
that the illustrations are too grotesque. 

17:21.790 --> 17:25.544
Ms. Ko's other books were also criticized
for being too cruel.

17:25.711 --> 17:28.422
I'm afraid the illustrations are adding
to that this time.

17:28.505 --> 17:31.258
- Right. Then we should--
- Just leave it the way it is.

17:32.092 --> 17:34.261
Yes, we'll just leave it the way it is.

17:34.344 --> 17:35.637
All right, what's next?

17:36.055 --> 17:39.391
About Ms. Ko's book that'll be adapted
into an animated film in the US…

17:39.475 --> 17:41.101
You mean, The Ugly Dog's Puppy?

17:41.185 --> 17:42.102
Right.

17:42.186 --> 17:44.063
They called and said

17:44.772 --> 17:47.357
that they want to change the dog character
to a cat.

17:47.441 --> 17:50.277
Tell them to keep it as is.
Otherwise, I'll annul the contract.

17:50.360 --> 17:53.697
Mun-yeong, then we'll suffer big losses...

17:54.198 --> 17:55.574
Then would you rather die?

17:56.909 --> 17:59.620
Seung-jae! You think
it's okay to turn a dog into a cat

17:59.703 --> 18:02.664
without the author's permission?
They're different species.

18:02.748 --> 18:05.000
Tell them to stick
to the original characters.

18:06.168 --> 18:07.294
Are you leaving?

18:10.005 --> 18:12.633
Make sure the signing event tomorrow
ends within an hour.

18:14.760 --> 18:17.179
The faster we get everything done,
the better.

18:19.098 --> 18:20.140
YOO SEUNG-JAE

18:20.557 --> 18:21.558
Okay, Seung-jae?

18:28.982 --> 18:29.817
Hello?

18:30.692 --> 18:33.278
Uncle, I need you to do
a background check on someone.

18:33.362 --> 18:36.865
I know a police officer
shouldn't do stuff like that.

18:36.949 --> 18:40.369
Then do you know anyone who works
at the National Intelligence Service

18:40.452 --> 18:42.162
or at a private detective agency--

18:43.247 --> 18:44.081
Hello?

18:46.333 --> 18:48.335
Gosh, what do I do?

18:52.089 --> 18:53.340
Thanks for your hard work.

18:53.715 --> 18:56.176
You're so capable.
I'm sad that you're leaving.

18:56.969 --> 18:57.803
Gang-tae.

18:59.221 --> 19:00.806
Someone's looking for you.

19:34.089 --> 19:35.215
You hurt your hand.

19:37.885 --> 19:39.553
I hurt it a little while working.

19:51.273 --> 19:52.649
I'm all sweaty.

19:58.322 --> 20:01.116
Jae-su told me
that I'd be able to find you here.

20:01.200 --> 20:02.242
I see.

20:03.410 --> 20:04.953
I heard you're moving again.

20:06.663 --> 20:09.416
You can leave whenever you want
without being attached.

20:09.791 --> 20:10.667
I envy you.

20:14.254 --> 20:16.256
Have you decided
which hospital to work at?

20:17.883 --> 20:19.259
I'm sure I'll find something.

20:20.594 --> 20:22.262
I'm not sure if it's good or bad,

20:22.596 --> 20:24.723
but new psychiatric hospitals
keep opening.

20:26.642 --> 20:29.144
My hospital is looking
for an experienced caregiver.

20:30.938 --> 20:32.856
It's called OK Psychiatric Hospital.

20:33.607 --> 20:34.983
Eight-hour rotating shifts.

20:35.067 --> 20:37.027
You'll get ten days off each month,

20:37.110 --> 20:40.614
so you can pick up a part-time job
on the side if you'd like.

20:40.697 --> 20:45.118
And you're a certified nursing assistant,
so you'll get extra pay.

20:46.370 --> 20:47.537
Where is the hospital?

20:47.996 --> 20:50.207
In Seongjin City, our hometown.

20:50.791 --> 20:53.543
You said you also lived there
when you were little.

20:53.627 --> 20:57.673
A bunch of areas have been redeveloped,
so it no longer has that small-town vibe.

20:58.257 --> 21:02.052
Also, a multiplex theater
opened recently and...

21:17.901 --> 21:19.695
Mom.

21:21.154 --> 21:23.198
Mom!

21:24.449 --> 21:26.410
Bring my mom back.

21:27.828 --> 21:29.079
Mom.

21:29.955 --> 21:31.832
Mom, no.

21:31.915 --> 21:34.293
- Mom, open your eyes.
- The butterfly did it.

21:34.376 --> 21:36.712
I mean, I saw it.

21:36.795 --> 21:37.796
- Mom!
- The butterfly…

21:38.714 --> 21:39.923
Mom, no.

21:40.007 --> 21:42.301
- Mom, please open your eyes.
- The butterfly

21:42.384 --> 21:43.927
killed Mom.

21:44.594 --> 21:45.846
The butterfly...

21:47.306 --> 21:50.142
The butterfly killed her.

21:50.892 --> 21:52.060
I saw it.

21:52.978 --> 21:54.271
The butterfly did it.

21:56.815 --> 21:59.192
Sang-tae! Tell us exactly what you saw.

21:59.276 --> 22:01.737
Was it a man or a woman? How old?

22:01.820 --> 22:04.489
What did this person look like?
Did you hear the voice?

22:04.573 --> 22:07.868
The butterfly said it'd kill me as well

22:08.660 --> 22:10.495
if I didn't keep my lips sealed.

22:11.079 --> 22:13.248
It said it'd chase me down

22:14.708 --> 22:17.169
and kill me!

22:19.588 --> 22:21.757
We should send the younger one
to a care center

22:22.341 --> 22:26.970
and his older brother to a center
that takes care of handicapped children.

22:28.138 --> 22:30.724
That would probably be best for them both.

22:31.350 --> 22:33.477
Okay. We'll leave him in your hands.

22:35.312 --> 22:36.563
Sang-tae, let's go.

22:41.443 --> 22:42.277
Come on.

22:53.288 --> 22:54.623
Where are we headed?

22:56.124 --> 22:58.126
To a place
where the butterfly can't find us.

23:00.545 --> 23:01.380
Somewhere far?

23:02.672 --> 23:03.673
Yes, far away.

23:29.282 --> 23:30.200
You must be tired.

23:32.327 --> 23:33.412
I could've come alone.

23:34.913 --> 23:37.082
Get on the bus. You'll arrive very late.

23:38.375 --> 23:39.209
Bye, then.

23:47.134 --> 23:48.468
Hey, Gang-tae.

23:49.302 --> 23:51.012
There's an empty room at my place.

23:52.055 --> 23:52.889
I mean...

23:53.974 --> 23:57.686
No one uses the room.
My mom and I only use the first floor.

23:59.479 --> 24:02.232
If you actually end up
moving back to Seongjin City,

24:02.649 --> 24:04.943
you won't have to look for a place.

24:08.447 --> 24:09.573
Bye now, for real.

24:18.915 --> 24:20.584
Thanks for your concern,

24:22.544 --> 24:23.628
but I won't go there.

24:24.296 --> 24:25.130
Why not?

24:27.841 --> 24:29.134
Because it's a countryside?

24:32.846 --> 24:33.680
Yes.

24:35.348 --> 24:36.183
That's why.

25:01.958 --> 25:03.877
Ju-ri, I don't know if you know this. 

25:06.254 --> 25:08.089
Gang-tae, that poor thing,

25:10.592 --> 25:13.011
never builds deep relationships.

25:13.470 --> 25:16.097
He'll leave eventually anyway,

25:16.389 --> 25:20.352
so he thinks it's pointless to build
a relationship that will only last a year.

25:29.986 --> 25:30.820
Why…

25:30.904 --> 25:31.738
Right,

25:33.907 --> 25:35.450
but why does he have to leave?

25:36.034 --> 25:37.202
It's because...

25:37.661 --> 25:38.620
What's the reason?

25:38.703 --> 25:41.081
You see, it's all...

25:44.459 --> 25:48.755
It's all because of that damn butterfly.

25:49.839 --> 25:50.674
Darn it.

25:54.761 --> 25:55.595
"Butterfly"?

26:08.692 --> 26:09.526
A butterfly?

26:29.671 --> 26:30.672
See you again.

26:31.590 --> 26:32.799
I don't think so.

26:56.823 --> 26:58.742
ORTHOPEDICS

27:00.410 --> 27:02.078
ORTHOPEDICS PHYSICAL THERAPIST

27:03.580 --> 27:05.790
JINCHEON, NORTH CHUNGCHEONG PROVINCE

27:21.890 --> 27:23.600
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

27:26.728 --> 27:29.689
DIRECTOR O JI-WANG
IS KOREA'S NUMBER ONE PTSD EXPERT

27:32.609 --> 27:35.487
DIRECTOR O SAID, "ONE MUST FACE
ONE'S TRAUMA TO OVERCOME IT"

27:52.504 --> 27:55.465
- "What do you want for Christmas?
- What do you want for Christmas?

27:55.548 --> 27:58.843
- A teddy bear? Cookies? Candy canes?
- A teddy bear? Cookies? Candy canes?

27:58.927 --> 28:00.178
- A doll?"
- A doll?

28:01.096 --> 28:03.890
- "Don't use separate products!
- Don't use separate products!

28:03.973 --> 28:07.936
- Take care of scalp and hair together.
- Take care of scalp and hair together.

28:08.395 --> 28:11.648
- Say goodbye to hair loss."
- Say goodbye to hair loss.

28:11.731 --> 28:13.441
No more hair loss!

28:14.818 --> 28:17.862
- "A true gentleman's scent."
- A true gentleman's scent.

28:18.279 --> 28:19.197
Be the cool guy.

28:23.910 --> 28:25.036
"Be the cool guy."

28:26.579 --> 28:30.458
I like Ms. Ko Mun-yeong! I like her!

28:32.836 --> 28:35.046
Jae-su, please...

28:38.550 --> 28:41.344
Don't worry, Gang-tae. You have me.

28:45.640 --> 28:47.016
GANG-TAE

28:48.977 --> 28:52.355
"Disinfect and eliminate odors
in one blow!"

28:52.439 --> 28:55.483
In one blow! Done!

28:55.817 --> 28:57.610
Right, Jae-su. When's he coming?

28:58.445 --> 29:00.697
Gosh, Jae-su...

29:01.406 --> 29:02.449
Jae-su.

29:02.991 --> 29:04.701
ZOMBIE KID

29:05.285 --> 29:07.120
KO MUN-YEONG BOOK SIGNING EVENT

29:07.203 --> 29:10.165
BOOK SIGNING EVENT THIS WAY

29:35.231 --> 29:37.233
My gosh, he's so tall.

29:37.317 --> 29:39.944
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

30:24.155 --> 30:25.949
Oh, no! It's cold!

30:36.167 --> 30:37.544
Sang-tae! Don't run!

30:38.169 --> 30:41.506
Look left and right. Be safe.
Safety comes first.

30:41.589 --> 30:43.925
Look at those blue pants. Blue jeans.

30:44.008 --> 30:45.385
I'm so happy now.

30:45.844 --> 30:46.970
My name is Lee Un-jae.

30:54.269 --> 30:55.353
Thank you.

30:57.480 --> 30:58.565
One, two…

31:10.952 --> 31:12.662
- Oh, is this it?
- My gosh!

31:13.288 --> 31:14.622
Gosh! What are you doing?

31:15.039 --> 31:16.165
- I'm sorry.
- All right.

31:20.461 --> 31:21.880
- Wait, Sang-tae.
- Yes.

31:21.963 --> 31:23.214
Sang-tae!

31:24.215 --> 31:25.592
- Listen up.
- Okay.

31:25.675 --> 31:28.136
- You see the restroom over there, right?
- Yes.

31:28.803 --> 31:29.888
- You see it?
- Yes.

31:30.388 --> 31:32.473
When you're getting her autograph later,

31:32.557 --> 31:35.101
I'll be watching you
from exactly that distance,

31:35.184 --> 31:37.562
- so get that woman's autograph--
- Ms. Ko Mun-yeong?

31:37.645 --> 31:39.480
Right. After you get Ms. Ko's autograph

31:39.564 --> 31:42.191
and take a picture with her,
we'll head home right away.

31:43.026 --> 31:45.361
- Then what will you get?
- The dinosaur encyclopedia.

31:46.988 --> 31:48.448
Don't run. Sang-tae!

31:49.032 --> 31:50.950
- Let's go.
- Slow down.

32:10.303 --> 32:11.304
- Sang-tae.
- What?

32:11.679 --> 32:12.680
Wait in line.

32:14.140 --> 32:15.391
- Wait here, okay?
- Okay.

32:16.059 --> 32:17.727
- I'll be over there.
- Okay.

32:19.270 --> 32:20.647
Okay, let's go.

32:22.357 --> 32:23.691
I'm getting her autograph.

32:32.825 --> 32:34.911
DO HUI-JAE'S POSTHUMOUS WORK

32:34.994 --> 32:37.538
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST

32:46.172 --> 32:47.840
WRITTEN BY DO HUI-JAE

32:53.805 --> 32:55.807
The mother is the queen
of detective fiction.

32:56.975 --> 32:58.643
Her daughter, children's literature.

32:59.102 --> 33:00.687
They're quite something.

33:03.022 --> 33:06.275
My goodness,
what brings a busy man like you here?

33:06.693 --> 33:09.112
I had to come to congratulate you
on the new release.

33:09.195 --> 33:12.991
As you know, I exclusively review
and critique Ko Mun-yeong's books.

33:13.408 --> 33:16.160
Right, that's true.

33:17.245 --> 33:20.999
Seven of her books are in the top ten list
of the best-selling children's books.

33:21.082 --> 33:22.083
BOOKS OF THE MONTH

33:22.166 --> 33:23.751
I have to say, it's impressive.

33:24.252 --> 33:26.671
Do you think
it's because of Ko Mun-yeong's looks?

33:26.754 --> 33:29.215
Gosh, come on.
It's not because of her looks.

33:29.298 --> 33:30.550
She's a great writer.

33:31.217 --> 33:33.302
All right, let's not stand around here.

33:33.386 --> 33:36.723
Why don't we go somewhere
and drink something sweet?

33:36.806 --> 33:38.766
- Let's go.
- Goodness, what's with you?

33:38.850 --> 33:41.102
Come on. It's okay.

33:42.478 --> 33:44.313
What's with you? I'm diabetic.

33:44.397 --> 33:47.316
Come on. You'll be fine. Excuse us.

34:07.462 --> 34:08.296
The sun is...

34:09.047 --> 34:11.883
What time is it? What? I'm late!

34:14.635 --> 34:16.137
What the fuck, 18 calls?

34:16.304 --> 34:18.014
I'm so dead.

34:18.431 --> 34:20.058
Shit, what do I do?

34:24.645 --> 34:25.938
Jeez.

34:29.067 --> 34:31.235
- Sang-tae, I have to take a call.
- Okay.

34:31.319 --> 34:32.487
- Stay right here.
- Okay.

34:40.912 --> 34:41.746
Gosh!

34:42.163 --> 34:45.249
My, it's a stegosaurus.
A real stegosaurus. Hi, stegosaurus.

34:45.333 --> 34:46.751
- A stegosaurus.
- My gosh.

34:46.834 --> 34:49.796
This is a stegosaurus.
It means "roofed lizard."

34:49.879 --> 34:51.255
You don't need to come.

34:51.339 --> 34:52.340
The plates.

34:52.423 --> 34:54.717
It's characterized
by the plates along the back.

34:54.801 --> 34:57.386
They probably lived
in the late Jurassic Period.

34:57.470 --> 34:59.138
- Scientists…
- What's wrong with him?

34:59.222 --> 35:00.181
What's with you?

35:00.264 --> 35:03.476
My gosh, this stegosaurus is huge!

35:03.559 --> 35:06.270
It has a small brain
despite its large size--

35:06.479 --> 35:07.814
Get lost!

35:09.190 --> 35:10.399
- My gosh.
- Oh, no!

35:10.483 --> 35:12.318
I have a toy that looks just like it.

35:12.401 --> 35:15.446
Here, this looks just like it.
This is my stegosaurus toy.

35:15.571 --> 35:19.158
Its name is Teary--

35:19.242 --> 35:20.952
- I've been too nice, right?
- My hair.

35:21.035 --> 35:22.120
- Get out.
- My hair.

35:22.203 --> 35:23.788
- My hair. Let go!
- Get out.

35:23.871 --> 35:25.206
- I said, get out!
- My hair...

35:25.289 --> 35:26.499
- Get out.
- No, my hair!

35:26.582 --> 35:27.959
Don't touch my hair!

35:28.042 --> 35:30.670
My hair... Don't touch my hair.

35:31.629 --> 35:33.256
My hair...

35:33.339 --> 35:36.092
Don't touch my hair.

35:36.175 --> 35:40.847
My hair! Don't touch my hair!

35:42.181 --> 35:43.891
Don't touch my hair. Go away!

35:50.523 --> 35:52.108
Sorry, excuse me.

35:57.280 --> 35:59.198
- No, my hair...
- Sang-tae, I'm sorry.

35:59.282 --> 36:00.950
- My hair...
- I'm sorry, Sang-tae.

36:01.033 --> 36:02.994
- You're okay now.
- I'm okay.

36:03.077 --> 36:05.997
- It's okay. I'm sorry.
- I'm okay.

36:06.080 --> 36:09.500
- You're okay now, Sang-tae.
- I'm okay now. I'm sorry.

36:09.584 --> 36:13.129
I'm okay now.

36:13.462 --> 36:15.298
I'm okay now. I'm sorry.

36:15.381 --> 36:16.215
It's okay.

36:16.716 --> 36:18.467
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

36:18.718 --> 36:19.719
Shall I help him?

36:21.929 --> 36:22.847
Or not?

36:25.558 --> 36:26.726
Shall I help him?

36:28.519 --> 36:29.645
Or not?

36:40.740 --> 36:41.991
Hey!

36:49.540 --> 36:50.666
You need to apologize.

36:54.795 --> 36:55.796
You.

36:56.964 --> 36:57.798
Apologize.

36:59.884 --> 37:03.137
- Why should I apologize to him?
- No, to me.

37:03.471 --> 37:04.305
What?

37:04.639 --> 37:07.725
You totally ruined my book signing event.

37:07.808 --> 37:09.727
Why is that my fault? This fucking--

37:10.478 --> 37:11.854
Goodness!

37:11.938 --> 37:13.606
Gosh!

37:13.689 --> 37:17.068
Who wouldn't scream when someone
grabs them by the hair like this?

37:20.071 --> 37:22.240
See? You're screaming too.

37:22.323 --> 37:24.242
Let go. I said, let go!

37:25.743 --> 37:27.954
- Let go.
- Listen.

37:28.037 --> 37:30.831
This lunatic was harassing our son.
What did you expect?

37:30.915 --> 37:32.166
Shit. I'm so screwed.

37:32.250 --> 37:34.919
Are you a psychiatrist?
How do you know he's a lunatic?

37:35.002 --> 37:36.087
Well, that's...

37:38.339 --> 37:40.675
I can tell because he kept rambling on

37:41.008 --> 37:42.969
about things that make no sense!

37:44.303 --> 37:45.471
Crazy bitch.

37:45.554 --> 37:47.390
- My gosh.
- Did she really say that?

37:47.515 --> 37:49.308
- What's with her?
- What did you say?

37:49.976 --> 37:53.145
Well, you kept rambling on
about things that make no sense,

37:54.063 --> 37:55.815
so I thought you were crazy.

37:58.192 --> 38:00.653
My gosh. Honey, you heard that, right?

38:00.945 --> 38:03.781
You all heard that, right?
She swore at me just now.

38:04.198 --> 38:05.992
What are you people doing? Record this!

38:06.075 --> 38:07.910
Yes! Record a video!

38:07.994 --> 38:10.663
- I'm speechless.
- Film this!

38:23.551 --> 38:27.680
I'm okay. I'm not a bad person.

38:28.806 --> 38:31.100
I'm okay. I'm not a bad person.

38:33.227 --> 38:35.896
I'm not a bad person.

38:35.980 --> 38:36.856
INVENTORY

38:43.904 --> 38:47.450
- Shouldn't you check on him?
- He'll let me in when he's calmed down.

38:47.867 --> 38:50.369
- When would that be?
- Usually in an hour.

38:51.162 --> 38:53.080
A day or two at the most.

38:59.003 --> 39:00.963
I have to stay here all night then?

39:04.133 --> 39:05.217
I never asked you to.

39:06.469 --> 39:08.596
Don't worry.
Just go sort out the situation.

39:08.679 --> 39:11.265
"Don't worry"?
Why would I worry? About whom?

39:18.230 --> 39:20.775
By the way, the back of his head
must be very sensitive.

39:21.275 --> 39:24.028
Is that his erogenous zone or something?

39:25.363 --> 39:26.739
Oh, it's like a detonator.

39:27.198 --> 39:30.409
When it's set off, the bomb goes off.
Then how does he get haircuts?

39:30.910 --> 39:34.205
Will he go like this again? "No!"

39:35.456 --> 39:36.832
Enough, okay?

39:38.834 --> 39:40.211
Now, you're looking at me.

40:00.815 --> 40:01.982
What are you doing?

40:03.275 --> 40:04.527
Don't wear hats.

40:06.070 --> 40:07.613
I can't see your pretty face.

40:14.453 --> 40:15.955
Why is your face turning red?

40:20.626 --> 40:22.878
Your forehead must be
your erogenous zone, right?

40:30.845 --> 40:32.972
Hey, Ms. Ko!

40:34.765 --> 40:36.016
You caused trouble again.

40:36.350 --> 40:39.311
Mr. Lee will be really stressed out
this time.

40:43.441 --> 40:45.401
Gosh, seriously!

40:45.484 --> 40:49.655
Why does she get herself in trouble
whenever I'm not around?

40:51.574 --> 40:54.702
She acts up
whenever that caregiver shows up.

40:54.785 --> 40:56.620
Hey, if you knew that,

40:56.704 --> 40:59.498
why didn't you make sure
they wouldn't run into each other?

40:59.582 --> 41:01.750
Gosh, why do I even pay you?

41:08.257 --> 41:10.426
Hi, Reporter Kim.

41:10.509 --> 41:13.012
Gosh, no. She never said, "Crazy bitch."

41:13.095 --> 41:15.431
She said,
"Gosh, this is driving me crazy."

41:15.514 --> 41:18.142
People mishear things all the time,
you know.

41:20.811 --> 41:22.062
That fucking prick.

41:25.232 --> 41:26.066
Your boyfriend?

41:26.484 --> 41:28.736
My gosh, you're dating?

41:29.612 --> 41:31.947
If you got those boxes,
just shut up and leave.

41:32.364 --> 41:35.868
Gosh, you look exactly like your mother
now that you have a frown face.

41:36.660 --> 41:38.913
Your mother was not only a great writer,

41:39.246 --> 41:41.624
but she was also very sexy.

41:43.000 --> 41:45.461
You have a lot in common with your mother.

41:50.174 --> 41:52.134
Cut the nonsense and just leave.

41:53.260 --> 41:54.970
Things might be great now,

41:56.305 --> 41:58.140
but I advise you to be careful.

41:59.141 --> 42:02.186
Her mother, who was a famous writer,

42:02.811 --> 42:04.396
suddenly passed away.

42:05.981 --> 42:08.275
And her father, a successful architect,
went nuts

42:09.235 --> 42:11.529
and got locked up
in a psychiatric hospital.

42:12.780 --> 42:15.449
Then what do you think will happen to you?

42:17.868 --> 42:20.371
You won't end up well
if you get involved with her.

42:22.206 --> 42:23.123
Keep that in mind.

42:35.636 --> 42:36.512
Let me go.

42:44.186 --> 42:45.020
Don't go.

42:51.652 --> 42:52.570
Do you like me?

42:55.030 --> 42:58.325
Are you going to look after me?
Do you think you can handle it?

42:58.576 --> 43:00.202
Who are you to stop me?

43:49.251 --> 43:50.085
I was right.

43:51.378 --> 43:52.755
I knew you'd come after me.

43:53.922 --> 43:56.634
I've been reading your books
for quite a long time now.

43:57.635 --> 43:58.802
You can easily see

43:58.886 --> 44:02.014
how that writer thinks and feels
through their writing.

44:03.474 --> 44:07.311
Then I guess you also know
what I'm going to do next.

44:10.147 --> 44:11.774
Don't mess with me.

44:12.232 --> 44:13.442
I won't go down alone.

44:14.109 --> 44:17.154
I'll take you and Mr. Lee down with me.

44:18.322 --> 44:20.658
Why do you think
they call me the Suicide Bomber?

44:21.325 --> 44:24.953
A jerk who never goes down
without taking others with you?

44:26.664 --> 44:29.667
I can destroy your career
with the tip of my pen.

44:29.958 --> 44:31.126
I'm sure you know that.

44:31.543 --> 44:33.962
A famous children's book writer

44:34.046 --> 44:35.964
actually turned out to have

44:36.298 --> 44:38.050
an antisocial personality disorder?

44:40.177 --> 44:42.596
What do you think will happen
when people find out?

44:46.975 --> 44:48.102
What do you want?

44:48.644 --> 44:50.896
I'm starting to get tired and bored

44:52.523 --> 44:53.774
of receiving these boxes.

44:55.275 --> 44:56.902
I think it'd be nice

44:59.446 --> 45:02.491
if you'd be kind enough to humor me

45:04.076 --> 45:04.910
a little.

45:15.921 --> 45:17.172
That's easy.

45:19.758 --> 45:20.676
But I, too,

45:28.058 --> 45:29.977
can attack you with the tip of my pen.

45:48.704 --> 45:49.997
Goodbye.

46:08.724 --> 46:09.600
911 EMERGENCY

46:11.268 --> 46:12.686
You evil bitch!

46:13.645 --> 46:18.066
You just wait! I swear I'll get rid of--

46:18.150 --> 46:19.485
Loosen your neck, sir.

46:25.532 --> 46:27.951
Damn, he should've just died.

46:28.035 --> 46:31.246
Why do all jerks have a long lifespan?

46:31.330 --> 46:32.331
Damn it.

46:32.956 --> 46:33.832
Stop right there.

46:39.046 --> 46:40.005
What are you doing?

46:41.423 --> 46:42.549
Take in a deep breath.

46:46.595 --> 46:47.429
Deeper.

46:51.600 --> 46:52.893
- What--
- Close your eyes.

46:59.983 --> 47:01.610
When you can't control yourself,

47:05.739 --> 47:07.783
cross your arms like this

47:08.200 --> 47:10.118
and take turns tapping on each shoulder.

47:13.455 --> 47:15.916
This will help you calm down.

47:19.837 --> 47:22.089
What is this?

47:23.173 --> 47:24.424
The Butterfly Hug Method.

47:31.139 --> 47:34.434
It's a self-healing technique
that's recommended for trauma patients.

47:43.193 --> 47:45.153
It's no fun to have you stand behind me.

47:52.619 --> 47:53.704
A trauma

47:54.872 --> 47:58.709
should be faced head-on like this
instead of handling it from behind.

48:37.372 --> 48:38.665
Why are you running away?

48:39.666 --> 48:40.876
I'm going to my brother.

48:40.959 --> 48:42.377
Slow down. My feet hurt.

48:43.754 --> 48:46.131
Hey.

48:46.548 --> 48:47.716
Hey!

48:51.178 --> 48:53.055
Don't make me get angry. I'll explode.

48:53.138 --> 48:54.681
That's why I taught you that.

48:54.765 --> 48:56.141
That stuff is useless.

48:57.559 --> 48:59.937
- I want you to be my safety pin.
- What?

49:00.437 --> 49:03.565
Keep me under control
so that I won't explode.

49:03.649 --> 49:06.735
You told me not to.
You told me I had no right to stop you.

49:06.818 --> 49:07.861
You hold grudges.

49:07.945 --> 49:09.196
Yes, that's right.

49:10.489 --> 49:13.742
So I'm giving you the right to be
Ko Mun-yeong's safety pin.

49:14.159 --> 49:17.412
- Why would I be your safety pin?
- Because you're a caregiver.

49:19.790 --> 49:22.167
Isn't it your job to care
for potential patients?

49:26.171 --> 49:27.172
Ask someone else.

49:28.674 --> 49:30.968
I'll pay you a lot.
How much do you want?

49:36.431 --> 49:39.434
We always say this to patients
who fully recover.

49:40.560 --> 49:41.395
What's that?

49:42.479 --> 49:44.022
"Hope I never see you again."

49:46.441 --> 49:47.275
Please.

49:49.361 --> 49:50.320
Let's not meet again.

49:51.655 --> 49:53.156
I really want you to stop.

49:53.657 --> 49:54.616
Stop following me.

50:06.795 --> 50:07.963
But I'm not a patient.

50:10.382 --> 50:11.842
"Hope I never see you again."

50:11.925 --> 50:14.845
That's what you say to your patients.
But I'm fine.

50:15.595 --> 50:16.430
You're right.

50:17.431 --> 50:19.349
You're different from patients.

50:20.142 --> 50:21.018
Exactly.

50:21.518 --> 50:23.645
Drugs and injections can't cure you.

50:24.855 --> 50:26.523
You were just born that way.

50:27.107 --> 50:30.402
So there's no way to treat you.
And you have a poor prognosis.

50:32.738 --> 50:33.613
It's just best

50:34.406 --> 50:35.949
to avoid people like you.

50:44.124 --> 50:45.333
You're not avoiding me.

50:46.084 --> 50:48.920
You're just running away
because you're scared.

50:52.924 --> 50:54.051
You coward.

51:18.658 --> 51:19.493
Hey.

51:50.065 --> 51:50.899
Do you

51:53.276 --> 51:54.111
still like me?

52:13.922 --> 52:14.840
Coward.

52:29.813 --> 52:30.647
Mun-yeong.

52:31.064 --> 52:33.316
How are you going to deal with this?

52:33.400 --> 52:35.569
There were tons of witnesses!

52:35.652 --> 52:38.738
Why are you always ruining
your own career?

52:38.822 --> 52:40.740
What were you doing? Were you smoking?

52:41.366 --> 52:42.909
- Yes.
- My gosh, come on.

52:42.993 --> 52:44.035
Mun-yeong!

52:44.119 --> 52:47.998
Why don't you just kill me?

52:57.132 --> 52:57.966
Sang-tae.

53:17.694 --> 53:19.946
Are you upset
that you didn't get her autograph?

53:23.200 --> 53:24.492
If you are upset,

53:26.453 --> 53:27.913
it makes my heart ache.

53:34.961 --> 53:37.214
- Gosh, my stomach.
- What's wrong?

53:37.297 --> 53:39.049
- My stomach…
- Your stomach, 911…

53:39.132 --> 53:40.258
- My stomach…
- Call 911.

53:40.800 --> 53:41.718
Surprise!

53:43.261 --> 53:44.512
The Dinosaur Encyclopedia.

53:44.971 --> 53:48.266
The Dinosaur Encyclopedia!

53:48.725 --> 53:50.143
The Dinosaur Encyclopedia!

53:52.062 --> 53:53.438
The Dinosaur Encyclopedia.

53:55.065 --> 53:55.899
Are you happy?

53:56.316 --> 53:58.360
Yes, I'm happy. I'm really happy.

54:01.488 --> 54:03.448
Who do you like more, me or Ko Mun-yeong?

54:04.032 --> 54:06.534
"Maiasaura means
'good mother reptile' in Latin.

54:06.993 --> 54:09.246
It's a herbivorous dinosaur
with a duck-like beak.

54:09.329 --> 54:11.748
Dromaeosaurus' name means
'swift running lizard,'

54:11.831 --> 54:13.917
and it got its name due to its fast speed.

54:14.000 --> 54:16.586
It's about 35cm big
when it hatches from the egg,

54:16.670 --> 54:19.881
and it grows up to three meters
in just a year. Maiasaura…

54:19.965 --> 54:23.593
Maiasauras lived in herds
and took care of their infants

54:23.677 --> 54:26.096
until they grew up to about one meter.

54:26.179 --> 54:29.724
Maisaura means 'good mother reptile.'

54:30.141 --> 54:32.435
Bagacera... Bagaceratops.

54:32.519 --> 54:36.356
It means 'small-horned face.'
Bagaceratops."

54:40.735 --> 54:41.820
What are you doing?

54:42.487 --> 54:43.738
Don't wear hats.

54:45.198 --> 54:46.908
I can't see your pretty face.

54:55.417 --> 54:57.043
It's a reptile.

54:58.795 --> 55:01.131
"Bagaceratops is a dinosaur with horns.

55:01.548 --> 55:04.718
It has a small body and short tail.

55:04.801 --> 55:07.304
Bagaceratops lived in the desert

55:07.387 --> 55:10.432
and dug holes in the sand
to lay eggs there.

55:10.515 --> 55:12.058
A dinosaur with small horns.

55:12.559 --> 55:15.020
A dinosaur with ghastly claws,

55:15.103 --> 55:17.230
Baryo... Baryonyx."

55:21.735 --> 55:22.569
PARAMEDIC

55:22.652 --> 55:25.447
Check his vitals and blood pressure
on your way there.

55:25.530 --> 55:28.616
- What about the epinephrine?
- I have some ready just in case.

55:28.908 --> 55:31.202
And the medication list
and medical history card?

55:31.453 --> 55:32.287
Here.

55:32.746 --> 55:34.414
Thanks. I'll be off now.

55:35.832 --> 55:36.666
Let's get going.

55:37.959 --> 55:38.793
Good luck.

55:46.009 --> 55:47.927
"It is very nimble and fast.

55:48.011 --> 55:49.596
Dromaeosaurus' name means

55:49.679 --> 55:51.556
- 'swift running lizard...'"
- Sang-tae.

55:51.639 --> 55:52.474
Sang-tae!

55:53.308 --> 55:54.309
"Its body and tail…"

55:54.392 --> 55:56.811
You shouldn't get distracted
when you're walking.

55:57.479 --> 55:59.981
Remember you got hit by a car
and got hospitalized?

56:02.108 --> 56:03.109
- Give it to me.
- No!

56:05.362 --> 56:07.947
Give me that. You can read it at home.

56:09.115 --> 56:10.116
- Come on.
- No.

56:10.200 --> 56:12.160
- It's dangerous.
- Look!

56:14.371 --> 56:17.082
- Sang-tae! Don't run.
- I'll be safe.

56:17.165 --> 56:19.209
- It's dangerous.
- Slowly.

56:22.212 --> 56:24.547
- Look.
- You can't fool me again. Give it to me.

56:24.631 --> 56:26.674
Jae-su. It's Jae-su.

56:46.569 --> 56:47.529
You know me, right?

56:48.738 --> 56:50.907
Even a ton of beer
can't make me get drunk.

56:52.784 --> 56:56.287
But it's weird how I get so easily drunk
whenever I drink with a woman.

56:57.372 --> 56:58.957
A long time ago,

56:59.833 --> 57:00.792
a wise man said,

57:01.709 --> 57:04.838
"History is made at night
with alcohol and a woman."

57:06.464 --> 57:07.590
But my history

57:10.385 --> 57:13.012
is going to be pitch dark.

57:14.973 --> 57:15.807
Utterly dark.

57:18.059 --> 57:19.936
- Jae-su.
- Yes?

57:21.229 --> 57:22.313
You should stop now.

57:22.814 --> 57:24.149
Stop what?

57:25.567 --> 57:27.318
Suffering from following us around.

57:32.740 --> 57:34.451
Settle down and live comfortably.

57:37.203 --> 57:38.997
Why do you care? That's up to me.

57:39.080 --> 57:40.790
Who are you to decide what I do?

57:40.874 --> 57:42.750
I'll decide whether to stop or not.

57:42.834 --> 57:44.294
What's the matter with you?

57:46.421 --> 57:47.672
Did something happen?

57:48.298 --> 57:49.674
Why are you so sentimental?

57:50.633 --> 57:52.260
That darn woman, Ko Mun-yeong.

57:52.343 --> 57:54.888
That crazy woman did something again,
didn't she?

57:56.181 --> 57:58.266
- No.
- Don't lie to me.

57:58.725 --> 58:01.853
- No, she didn't.
- She obviously did.

58:01.936 --> 58:03.938
You never mean it when you say "no."

58:04.022 --> 58:04.981
What did she do?

58:09.235 --> 58:10.570
I thought I was on the run

58:12.906 --> 58:14.449
because of my brother.

58:15.450 --> 58:16.743
The butterflies and all.

58:18.203 --> 58:20.997
I thought we were being chased
by something that doesn't exist

58:23.333 --> 58:24.918
all because of Sang-tae.

58:26.127 --> 58:27.086
Well, it's true.

58:28.421 --> 58:30.006
But today, for the first time,

58:31.216 --> 58:32.258
I thought

58:34.594 --> 58:36.262
maybe I was just running away

58:38.890 --> 58:40.892
because I wanted to.

58:43.019 --> 58:44.020
That's not true.

58:47.565 --> 58:48.399
You see,

58:51.402 --> 58:53.321
when life is unbearably hard,

58:57.116 --> 58:58.618
the easiest way out is to run.

59:29.941 --> 59:31.359
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES 

59:32.110 --> 59:34.445
This is Ms. Ko Mun-yeong's book.

59:36.823 --> 59:38.533
Ko Mun-yeong.

59:38.616 --> 59:43.162
Sang-tae, do you remember
where we used to live when we were young?

59:48.376 --> 59:50.753
- Where we used to live with Mom.
- Seongjin City.

59:52.463 --> 59:53.298
Right.

59:57.927 --> 59:58.803
Should we

01:00:01.723 --> 01:00:02.849
go live there?

01:00:06.519 --> 01:00:08.271
- If you don't want to--
- Sure.

01:00:17.238 --> 01:00:18.239
Are you really okay?

01:00:19.115 --> 01:00:22.118
The Chinese restaurant there
sells really good jjamppong.

01:00:22.201 --> 01:00:25.705
It's at the entrance of the market.
It has mussels and chili pepper in it.

01:00:25.788 --> 01:00:27.624
- The broth tastes amazing.
- Sang-tae.

01:00:28.791 --> 01:00:29.667
It's the best.

01:00:32.503 --> 01:00:34.339
You're really brave.

01:00:35.673 --> 01:00:36.966
I'm a coward.

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:40.511
You're the younger brother.
That's why you're a coward.

01:00:41.054 --> 01:00:43.222
Because you're the younger brother.

01:00:43.556 --> 01:00:46.643
Trust me. I'm the older brother,
you can count on me.

01:00:47.226 --> 01:00:49.228
Trust me. You can trust me.

01:01:04.327 --> 01:01:06.162
- That's such a relief.
- Yes.

01:01:08.915 --> 01:01:12.210
Who is that?
Is he your boyfriend in Seoul?

01:01:13.544 --> 01:01:15.213
- What?
- Go ahead and pick up.

01:01:15.296 --> 01:01:16.631
MOON GANG-TAE

01:01:18.174 --> 01:01:19.008
Hello?

01:01:21.427 --> 01:01:22.303
Hello?

01:01:23.554 --> 01:01:24.389
Hey.

01:01:29.018 --> 01:01:29.852
Yes.

01:01:55.294 --> 01:01:56.713
BORN IN SEONGJIN CITY

01:01:57.839 --> 01:01:59.424
"Seongjin City"?

01:02:11.227 --> 01:02:12.937
No wonder.

01:02:13.187 --> 01:02:16.941
Your eyes remind me of
someone I used to know.

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:26.993
SANGSANGESANG PUBLISHERS

01:02:27.076 --> 01:02:28.578
We know nothing about it.

01:02:28.661 --> 01:02:30.496
It was a misunderstanding. All rumors.

01:02:30.580 --> 01:02:32.790
We can't reach Ms. Ko either.

01:02:33.374 --> 01:02:34.542
Yes. Just a second.

01:02:35.793 --> 01:02:37.712
- Hello?
- This fucking dumbass--

01:02:37.795 --> 01:02:39.714
KO MUN-YEONG ABUSES
AND SWEARS AT A FAN

01:02:40.298 --> 01:02:41.132
My goodness.

01:02:43.176 --> 01:02:45.344
- Let go of me.
- Listen.

01:02:45.678 --> 01:02:48.973
This lunatic was harassing our son.
What did you expect?

01:02:49.223 --> 01:02:50.141
Crazy bitch.

01:02:51.058 --> 01:02:52.769
I thought you were crazy.

01:02:54.353 --> 01:02:55.563
Didn't you...

01:02:56.189 --> 01:02:59.400
collect all the CCTV footage
from the bookstore?

01:02:59.484 --> 01:03:02.862
This video was uploaded this morning
on an online mothers' forum.

01:03:02.945 --> 01:03:05.907
- Ko Mun-yeong abused and swore at a fan
- My goodness.

01:03:05.990 --> 01:03:08.367
at her own book signing event

01:03:08.451 --> 01:03:12.163
and made her fans get extremely shocked
and disappointed at her.

01:03:12.663 --> 01:03:15.917
She suddenly asked me to apologize
and started yanking my hair.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:17.418
I already have hair loss.

01:03:17.835 --> 01:03:18.795
"Crazy bitch."

01:03:20.296 --> 01:03:23.216
She called me that and started laughing.
It creeped me out.

01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:26.844
Ever since then,
I've been getting nightmares.

01:03:27.470 --> 01:03:29.263
Everyone, stay focused.

01:03:29.347 --> 01:03:32.767
I think we should visit them
and compensate them for what happened.

01:03:32.850 --> 01:03:34.310
That is not all.

01:03:35.061 --> 01:03:38.648
After the recent incident,
Ko Mun-yeong's bizarre past

01:03:38.731 --> 01:03:41.108
went viral online.

01:03:41.526 --> 01:03:43.986
KO MUN-YEONG’S BIZARRE PAST ACTIONS
SHOCK HER FANS

01:03:44.445 --> 01:03:45.321
Read it out loud.

01:03:50.409 --> 01:03:51.410
Don't you know this?

01:03:51.744 --> 01:03:52.745
Oh, right.

01:03:52.829 --> 01:03:55.081
What do you brats think a fairy tale is?

01:03:55.164 --> 01:03:56.791
The brat on the back. You tell me.

01:03:56.874 --> 01:03:58.960
- What did she say?
- Did I hear it wrong?

01:03:59.043 --> 01:04:01.295
- Don't you know?
- It's okay, everyone.

01:04:01.379 --> 01:04:04.674
It's how she calls all kids.
Not a big deal.

01:04:04.757 --> 01:04:06.884
- Kids are cute. Cute brats.
- What?

01:04:06.968 --> 01:04:08.678
What's the issue here?

01:04:08.761 --> 01:04:11.764
- It's used in an affectionate way.
- Are you kidding me?

01:04:11.848 --> 01:04:13.015
Lovable brats, right?

01:04:13.099 --> 01:04:15.601
- What's the matter?
- People are raising an issue about

01:04:15.685 --> 01:04:18.521
the famed fairy tale writer
who has instilled dreams and hopes

01:04:18.604 --> 01:04:21.399
to many kids around the world.

01:04:21.482 --> 01:04:25.319
Meanwhile, some even say
her name should be removed

01:04:25.403 --> 01:04:28.990
from the list of candidates
for the Hans Christian Andersen Award--

01:04:34.245 --> 01:04:35.371
I... Well...

01:04:36.122 --> 01:04:37.164
What should we do?

01:04:37.248 --> 01:04:39.625
I don't think money can solve this one.

01:04:39.709 --> 01:04:41.961
No, that's not true.

01:04:42.044 --> 01:04:43.629
It's okay, you guys.

01:04:43.713 --> 01:04:45.673
We've been through worse.

01:04:45.756 --> 01:04:48.801
- There has to be a way out.
- Sir!

01:04:49.719 --> 01:04:50.970
We're in trouble.

01:04:51.053 --> 01:04:53.598
Why? What is it this time?

01:04:53.681 --> 01:04:57.351
A civic group applied for an injunction
against selling the new book, Zombie Kid,

01:04:57.602 --> 01:05:00.187
saying the storyline and illustration
are too cruel.

01:05:03.608 --> 01:05:05.860
Where is Mun-yeong right now?

01:05:06.193 --> 01:05:08.905
Where is Ko Mun-yeong?

01:05:38.059 --> 01:05:39.602
WELCOME TO OJI-GUN, SEONGJIN CITY

01:05:48.152 --> 01:05:49.528
Where is Mun-yeong?

01:05:49.946 --> 01:05:51.989
She checked out of her hotel room.

01:05:53.866 --> 01:05:55.743
Oh, okay. Then I should

01:05:57.036 --> 01:05:58.663
also check out from my life.

01:05:58.746 --> 01:06:00.706
- Mom!
- Sir!

01:06:00.790 --> 01:06:01.916
- No!
- Catch him!

01:06:01.999 --> 01:06:03.542
Mom!

01:06:03.626 --> 01:06:05.419
Sir! Stop him!

01:06:05.503 --> 01:06:07.380
Sir! No, sir!

01:06:07.463 --> 01:06:08.798
Sir, stop!

01:06:08.881 --> 01:06:10.591
Mr. Lee!

01:06:13.844 --> 01:06:14.887
I think

01:06:16.597 --> 01:06:18.349
it's all because of me.

01:06:20.726 --> 01:06:21.560
What?

01:06:22.228 --> 01:06:23.062
To be honest,

01:06:23.521 --> 01:06:27.024
I sent this to Ms. Ko this morning.

01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:37.702
INFORMATION ON MOON GANG-TAE

01:06:39.453 --> 01:06:40.663
"Moon Gang-tae"?

01:06:41.706 --> 01:06:42.832
The caregiver?

01:06:43.666 --> 01:06:46.419
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:13.112
There we go.

01:08:00.367 --> 01:08:02.286
MR. LEE

01:08:03.829 --> 01:08:05.122
ANSWER

01:08:05.956 --> 01:08:08.459
Mun-yeong, where are you?
Tell me where you are!

01:08:09.794 --> 01:08:13.005
Do you know The Red Shoes
written by Hans Christian Andersen?

01:08:13.506 --> 01:08:15.382
What are you talking about?

01:08:15.466 --> 01:08:17.134
Where are you right now?

01:08:17.218 --> 01:08:20.471
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

01:08:22.014 --> 01:08:23.390
It's raining.

01:08:23.474 --> 01:08:25.267
- It's raining.
- Let's go inside.

01:08:25.351 --> 01:08:28.229
- It's raining.
- Let's go inside.

01:08:28.312 --> 01:08:29.897
Don't run.

01:08:29.980 --> 01:08:32.024
- Be careful.
- Let's go inside.

01:08:34.193 --> 01:08:36.612
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

01:09:01.011 --> 01:09:05.558
The little girl wore her red shoes
everywhere she went,

01:09:06.725 --> 01:09:09.895
even to a God-fearing church.

01:09:23.033 --> 01:09:24.618
Once you wear those shoes,

01:09:25.661 --> 01:09:28.247
your feet start dancing on their own.

01:09:29.540 --> 01:09:31.709
And you can never stop dancing

01:09:32.543 --> 01:09:35.129
or take off those shoes.

01:09:36.463 --> 01:09:37.339
But even so,

01:09:38.340 --> 01:09:41.635
the little girl
never gave up on those red shoes.

01:09:43.929 --> 01:09:46.765
In the end, the executioner

01:09:46.849 --> 01:09:48.851
had to cut off her feet.

01:09:50.394 --> 01:09:54.106
But the two feet that got cut off

01:09:55.191 --> 01:09:57.234
still continued to dance
in those red shoes.

01:09:58.235 --> 01:09:59.862
Some things can't be torn apart

01:09:59.945 --> 01:10:02.198
no matter how hard you try to do so.

01:10:10.122 --> 01:10:11.207
Don't tell me...

01:10:13.667 --> 01:10:15.461
Yes, the ones in the rooms are fine.

01:10:15.544 --> 01:10:18.464
But the lights in the lobby
and the reception area are out.

01:10:20.341 --> 01:10:21.550
Yes, okay.

01:10:29.934 --> 01:10:31.018
That is why

01:10:32.269 --> 01:10:35.481
obsession is noble and beautiful.

01:10:59.463 --> 01:11:00.339
I have

01:11:02.424 --> 01:11:05.261
finally found my red shoes.

01:11:30.536 --> 01:11:31.370
Why

01:11:33.122 --> 01:11:34.164
are you here?

01:11:35.374 --> 01:11:36.292
Why do you think?

01:11:37.376 --> 01:11:38.836
I came because I missed you.

01:12:37.603 --> 01:12:39.271
How can you define a relationship

01:12:40.272 --> 01:12:43.192
in just one word?

01:12:44.234 --> 01:12:46.153
Please teach a class, Ms. Ko.

01:12:46.236 --> 01:12:49.156
I'm Ko Mun-yeong.
I'll be teaching this writing class.

01:12:49.239 --> 01:12:51.158
I have no time to play with you.

01:12:52.159 --> 01:12:54.495
Hypocrite. I know you want some fun.

01:12:55.120 --> 01:12:56.538
I forget things these days.

01:12:56.997 --> 01:12:58.290
Even Sang-tae.

01:13:00.626 --> 01:13:02.461
- You're not running away.
- You're making

01:13:04.588 --> 01:13:06.173
me worried.
